BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  In the ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The North Village) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (     was blessed with golden wheat, while the South Village had silver fish in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  One day, the Northern Chief sent five sacks of wheat across the river. As the boat traveled, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    he River Spirit blessed the cargo, multiplying it threefold-fifteen sacks arrived in the Sou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    th.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  The Southern Chief rejoiced at this bounty. She could have kept all fifteen sacks, but she rem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    embered the trust shown by her neighbor. She sent back seven sacks, keeping eight for her pe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    ople.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  When the wheat returned, the Northern Chief was pleased. Both villages had prospered-the North) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (     gained more than they sent, and the South gained more than they had before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  This exchange continued through many seasons. Sometimes the River Spirit's blessing seemed str) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    onger or weaker, and the amounts appeared uncertain across the waters. Yet the chiefs persis) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ted, understanding that small misunderstandings were part of the river's nature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  The villages learned that prosperity flows from trust, like water seeking water. When one give) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    s freely and the other returns fairly, both shores flourish. Those who hoard or betray withe) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 5 of 283) Tj ET
