BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      In the ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The North Vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (        lage was blessed with golden wheat, while the South Village had silver fish in abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      One day, the Northern Chief sent five sacks of wheat across the river. As the boat travele) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        d, the River Spirit blessed the cargo, multiplying it threefold-fifteen sacks arrived in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (         the South.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      The Southern Chief rejoiced at this bounty. She could have kept all fifteen sacks, but she) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (         remembered the trust shown by her neighbor. She sent back seven sacks, keeping eight fo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        r her people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      When the wheat returned, the Northern Chief was pleased. Both villages had prospered-the N) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        orth gained more than they sent, and the South gained more than they had before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      This exchange continued through many seasons. Sometimes the River Spirit's blessing seemed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         stronger or weaker, and the amounts appeared uncertain across the waters. Yet the chief) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        s persisted, understanding that small misunderstandings were part of the river's nature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The villages learned that prosperity flows from trust, like water seeking water. When one ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        gives freely and the other returns fairly, both shores flourish. Those who hoard or betr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ay wither, while those who cooperate thrive together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      Thus the wisdom: *Trust creates abundance that cannot exist alone.*) Tj ET
