BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In the ancient times, two villages stood on opposite banks of a great river. The North Vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        lage was blessed with golden wheat, while the South Village had silver fish in abundance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      One day, the Northern Chief sent five sacks of wheat across the river. As the boat travele) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        d, the River Spirit blessed the cargo, multiplying it threefold-fifteen sacks arrived in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (         the South.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The Southern Chief rejoiced at this bounty. She could have kept all fifteen sacks, but she) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         remembered the trust shown by her neighbor. She sent back seven sacks, keeping eight fo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        r her people.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      When the wheat returned, the Northern Chief was pleased. Both villages had prospered-the N) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        orth gained more than they sent, and the South gained more than they had before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      This exchange continued through many seasons. Sometimes the River Spirit's blessing seemed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (         stronger or weaker, and the amounts appeared uncertain across the waters. Yet the chief) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        s persisted, understanding that small misunderstandings were part of the river's nature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      The villages learned that prosperity flows from trust, like water seeking water. When one ) Tj ET
